    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-83549",
      "publishedDate": "2026-09-01T21:28:50.717Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-09-02T19:58:25.220Z",
      "description": "Post-authentication Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection') vulnerability has been identified in the SMA1000 Appliance Management Console (AMC) which in specific conditions could potentially enable a remote authenticated attacker as administrator to execute arbitrary OS commands, resulting in remote code execution.",
      "severity": "8.5",
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：SonicWall SMA1000 Appliances\n🔓 漏洞类型：OS Command Injection (CWE-78)\n⚠️ **已在 CISA KEV 中标记为已知被利用 — 请立即修复！**\n📊 官方评级：HIGH (CVSS 8.5)\n📝 SonicWall SMA1000 Appliances contains an OS command injection vulnerability that could enable a remote authenticated attacker as administrator to execute arbitrary OS commands, resulting in remote code execution.\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
      "references": [
        {
          "url": "https://psirt.global.sonicwall.com/vuln-detail/SNWLID-2026-0016",
          "type": "reference"
        }
      ],
